<% content_for :title, "Carline Report - #{Profile.current.name}" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <style>
    @media print {
      header, footer, .no-print { display: none !important; }
      main { max-width: 100% !important; padding: 0 !important; }
    }
  </style>
<% end %>

<div class="no-print flex items-center justify-between mb-8 flex-wrap gap-2">
  <%= link_to "← Back to the analysis", carline_path, class: "text-sm text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800" %>
  <%= link_to "Download PDF ↓", carline_report_path(format: :pdf), class: "text-sm font-medium bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white rounded-lg px-4 py-2" %>
</div>

<p class="text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-600 tracking-wide uppercase mb-2">Carline, data-driven</p>
<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Executive Summary</h1>
<p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-10">
  Generated <%= Date.current.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %> · Illustrative data, real methodology
  (see the full page for the disclosure).
</p>

<div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-12">
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @avg_wait %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">avg. wait, minutes</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @worst_day&.worst_wait_minutes %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">worst single wait</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @complaint_count %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">complaints logged</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
    <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-indigo-600"><%= @days.count %></p>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-1">dismissals observed</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="mb-10 max-w-2xl">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Finding 1 - baseline, not a point average</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
    Wait time decays over the school-year adoption period, then stabilizes. The stabilized value is
    the honest baseline to plan against, <strong><%= @plateau_baseline %> minutes</strong>, not the
    elevated average from the decay period.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-10 max-w-2xl">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">Finding 2 - the reframe</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
    <strong><%= @vocal_bus_ready_percent %>%</strong> of repeat-complaint families are already
    extended-day families who've separately said they want a bus -
    <strong><%= @bus_ready_families.count %></strong> families total (of <%= @total_families %>)
    would take a bus today. Complaint frequency correlates with bus-readiness rather than being
    randomly distributed across the population, which reframes part of the problem from pure
    carline throughput to unmet transport demand.
  </p>
  <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 italic">
    Honest caveat: a real 95% confidence interval at a ±5% margin needs roughly 384 families
    surveyed; this sample has <%= @vocal_families.size %>. This page sketches the method, it isn't
    a finished study.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-10">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-4">Three independent levers, not mutually exclusive</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-700 text-left">
          <th class="p-3 font-semibold rounded-l-lg">Option</th>
          <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Approach</th>
          <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Effort</th>
          <th class="p-3 font-semibold">Timeline</th>
          <th class="p-3 font-semibold rounded-r-lg">Effect</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-slate-700">
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-200">
          <td class="p-3 font-medium">A</td>
          <td class="p-3">Earlier, organized check-in</td>
          <td class="p-3">Low-medium</td>
          <td class="p-3">Weeks</td>
          <td class="p-3">~15% wait reduction</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-slate-200">
          <td class="p-3 font-medium">B</td>
          <td class="p-3">Stagger dismissal by grade</td>
          <td class="p-3">Medium</td>
          <td class="p-3">Weeks</td>
          <td class="p-3">~20% wait reduction</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="p-3 font-medium">C</td>
          <td class="p-3">Afternoon bus route for bus-ready families</td>
          <td class="p-3">High</td>
          <td class="p-3">A semester</td>
          <td class="p-3"><%= @bus_ready_families.count %> cars removable</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<p class="text-xs text-slate-400 border-t border-slate-200 pt-4">
  resumeonrails.com/carline · Kaleigh Unger
</p>
